# Auto-deploy after changes

When you finish a set of code or asset changes that affect the running app (Worker, web SPA, MCP, styles, public assets), deploy before ending the turn:

```bash
npm run deploy
```

That builds `web` and runs `wrangler deploy`.

## When to deploy

- Default: **yes** after implementing or fixing something user-facing or API-facing.
- Skip only if: the user said not to deploy, the change is docs/rules-only with no runtime impact, deploy already failed and needs a fix first, or you only answered a question with no edits.

## After deploy

Report the live URL (`https://vibehub.devpost67.workers.dev`) and version ID briefly. Do not ask whether to deploy unless something is unsafe (destructive migrations, secrets, etc.).
